 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Memory Consumption:** High, especially for real scenes [S1].
-*   **Training Speed:** Slow, approximately one day per scene on GeForce RTX 3090 [S1].
-*   **Coarse Stage Importance:** Removing the coarse stage causes significant performance drop because the voxel grid covers a bigger space without proxy geometry filtering [S1].
-*   **Inpaint Network Importance:** Removing the inpaint network significantly reduces performance (e.g., Hell Warrior PSNR drops from 27.71 to 27.15) [S1].
-*   **Splatting Choice:** Softmax splatting with predicted weights showed no obvious improvement and introduced too much complexity compared to average splatting [S1].
+*   **Memory Consumption:** High memory usage, especially for real scenes [S1].
+*   **Training Speed:** Slow training time (~1 day per scene on RTX 3090) [S1].
+*   **Coarse Stage Necessity:** Removing the coarse stage causes significant performance drops because the voxel grid covers a larger space without proxy geometry filtering [S1].
+*   **Inpainting Importance:** Removing the inpaint network significantly reduces performance (e.g., Hell Warrior PSNR drops from 27.71 to 27.15) [S1].
+*   **Canonical Time Selection:** Setting canonical time to the middle frame improves performance for HyperNeRF as the geometry is closer to other time steps [S1].
 
